# Coolify: MCP + CLI

Anything Coolify (apps, services, databases, deploys, env, logs, servers, domains, health) goes through **`user-coolify` MCP** and **`coolify` CLI**. Do not open the Coolify UI, SSH into the host, or raw-curl the Coolify API.

## MCP (`user-coolify`)

`GetMcpTools` on `user-coolify` first, then `CallMcpTool`. Typical tools: `list_applications`, `get_application`, `deploy`, `logs`, `env_vars`, `list_databases`, `diagnose_app`. Env values stay masked unless you explicitly need `reveal`.

```text
❌ BAD  open Coolify dashboard / ssh root@vps / curl https://coolify.../api/...
✅ GOOD GetMcpTools({ server: "user-coolify" }) then CallMcpTool deploy / logs / env_vars
```

`user-coolify-backup-mcp` only for backup/restore. Not a substitute for app/deploy/log work.

## CLI (`coolify`)

Binary: `/usr/local/bin/coolify`. This repo uses the default context (no `--context`). Prefer `--format json` when parsing.

```text
coolify app list
coolify app get <uuid>
coolify deploy <uuid>
coolify database list
```

MCP first when a tool exists. CLI for commands MCP lacks, scripting, or when MCP is down. Same source of truth — do not mix guessed UUIDs from chat memory; list, then act.
